    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "Reconstruction of the statue of Pharaoh Taharqua (690-665 BC). Height 2.70 m. The original statues of the Kushite pharaohs were smashed during the offensive (655 BC) of Pharaoh Psammetichus I (664-610 BC), but collected and buried in Doukki Gel. Rediscovered in 2003 and reconstituted but untransportable, a copy was made in 3D printing for the Pharaoh of the Two Lands exhibition.",
